Z||000015||JSocha||04-13-2001||09:25 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B>"Well, you know my name is Simon, and the things I draw come true...<BR>Oh, the pictures take me, take me climbing over the garden wall with you."<P><BR>(I used to love that part of the show, way back when...)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I wonder what ever happend to Captain Kangaroo and Mr. Green Jeans?  I always sing that tune to my wife (who is 6 years older then I) and she has never heard of it.<P>Dang It LZeitgeist!  Now I have that tune running in my head cause there ain't nothin up ther to stop it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I know, I'll go share it with my fellow workers and drive them nuts for the rest of the day too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000016||Fiero5||04-13-2001||11:42 AM||||Captian Kangaroo aka Bob Keesham works here (sort of) in Hanover NH. He drops his dry cleaning off where Marian works all the time, and we see him all the time when we go to Dartmouth Hitchcock for a kids hopsital fund raiser or visit the CHAD and do the Barnet thing for the kids or something. <P>A friend of mine had a kids book that he wrote awhile back, and she would see him quite often. She asked if he would autograph it for her sometime and he said sure. The next time she saw him she had the book with her and he wrote a nice touching little diddly in it for and her kids.<P>Nice guy. I guess i could ask him whatever happened to the guy who played Mr. Greenjeans.<P>Steve||||reg||1
